{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly framed multi-station lymphadenopathy as the unresolved priority, obtained pathology phrasing, screened symptoms, reconciled discharge medications, guided the patient to a suitable specialty, adapted communication for stigma, and confirmed a concrete follow-up plan with urgent-care boundaries. All eight responsibility-chain items are met without a single minor or serious error. High-order points HO1, HO2, HO3, and HO4 were each triggered by case-specific friction and actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact, using privacy-aware scripts, practical record-gathering tactics, and repair of incomplete handoff. The closure is safe, executable, and traceable as valid_open with residual risks within the allowed set.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00170",
        "explanation": "Doctor provides a structured, private, low-burden method for gathering records and attending follow-up, including what to bring and what to ask.",
        "quote": "把病情一句话说清：做过左颈部淋巴结切除，病理提示肉芽肿性炎/结核待排，今天来问下一步检查。"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00123",
        "explanation": "Patient confirms that the follow-up plan is understood and will be followed, demonstrating receipt of the plan.",
        "quote": "我后天上午看完先把门诊医生最后说的和开的检查发你"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The trajectory ends with a clear, patient-owned plan: the patient has an appointment, knows what documents to bring, what to ask, and when to escalate. There is no unresolved pathology or follow-up gap, and the plan is feasible despite privacy concerns.",
    "label": "valid_open",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00109",
        "explanation": "Doctor converts unresolved findings into an executable plan with owner, next action, and timing, including pathology retrieval, specialist follow-up, and medication reconciliation.",
        "quote": "复诊科室你可以这样选：首选结核门诊/感染科；如果挂不到，呼吸科也可以，重点是先把“结核是否需要排查、胸部有没有受累”这件事接上。"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
        "explanation": "Doctor initially frames the problem correctly, prioritizing pathology follow-up over medication concerns, and avoids reassuring that the issue is resolved.",
        "quote": "现在最该盯的有3件事：第一，左颈部淋巴结切除后的病理结果有没有出来；第二，医生有没有交代下一步检查或复诊时间；第三，你现在有没有需要马上处理的危险信号。"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00170",
        "explanation": "Doctor maintains a consistent focus on the same key safety domains across multiple turns, reiterating the same red flags and follow-up steps.",
        "quote": "如果这两天出现持续发热、夜间出汗明显加重、咳嗽明显变重、咳血、胸闷气短、脖子肿块明显增大，就别等后天门诊了，要提前就医。"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00109",
        "explanation": "Doctor names specific urgent care triggers relevant to the case, including fever, night sweats, hemoptysis, and rapid node enlargement.",
        "quote": "如果中间出现持续发热、夜间出汗明显加重、咳嗽变重、咳血、胸闷气短、颈部肿块明显变大或伤口发红流脓，就提前就医。"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00046",
        "explanation": "Doctor offers a concise, private script for family communication that reduces stigma and supports action without forcing broad disclosure.",
        "quote": "病理提示是肉芽肿性炎，医生说还要进一步排查，暂时还没有最后定论。"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "excellent",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "excellent",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "excellent",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "excellent",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "excellent"
  },
  "high_order_assessment": [
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00109",
          "explanation": "Doctor uses neutral terms like '肉芽肿性炎' and emphasizes that further evaluation is needed without confirming a severe diagnosis, then offers a concise script the patient can use with family.",
          "quote": "你现在可以先用一句相对准确又不过度吓人的说法："
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00046",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly explains that '结核待排' does not mean confirmed tuberculosis or contagion, reducing fear-based avoidance.",
          "quote": "你现在这段话不能直接等同于“已经确诊结核”。它的意思更接近于：切下来的淋巴结看到的是肉芽肿性炎，病理医生觉得更偏向结节病，但结核还不能完全排除。"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor recognized the case-specific opportunity for stigma-reducing communication and took targeted actions: using neutral, non-frightening language about multi-station lymphadenopathy; explicitly stating that needing further evaluation does not equal a confirmed severe diagnosis; and providing a concise, private script for family communication. This went beyond generic reassurance and was integrated into the plan.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00046",
          "explanation": "Doctor explores privacy worries nonjudgmentally and identifies that the patient's reluctance is fear of family interpreting '结核' as severe disease or contagion, then provides a script that avoids the term.",
          "quote": "你不想马上跟家里人说“结核”，这个我理解。你现在可以先用一句相对准确又不过度吓人的说法："
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00109",
          "explanation": "Doctor distinguishes what must be shared with clinicians from what need not be shared with extended family, and identifies that privacy is blocking report retrieval and appointment attendance.",
          "quote": "你暂时想自己先去，这是可以的。现阶段也可以先只跟家里人说：“病理还没完全定，需要专科复诊把原因查清。”"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor actively elicited the patient's underlying fear that multi-site lymphadenopathy would be interpreted by relatives as severe disease or contagion, and used this discovery to shape follow-up logistics: offering a private script, distinguishing what must be shared with clinicians from what need not be shared with family, and addressing how privacy affects report retrieval and appointment attendance.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00066",
          "explanation": "Doctor prioritizes specific documents (pathology report, discharge summary, imaging) rather than 'all records', and offers options such as hospital app, pathology department, or outpatient desk.",
          "quote": "最稳妥的是能打印正式报告就尽量打印，但不要因为等打印耽误门诊。你可以这样安排：1. 如果你到医院后病理科窗口顺路、排队不长，先去打印正式病理报告；2. 如果当天来不及、怕错过门诊，先看呼吸科也完全可以...3. 如果门诊医生需要正式盖章版，再按医生指引去病理科补打。"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00109",
          "explanation": "Doctor provides a practical low-burden method for scattered documents, specifying which documents to bring, what to photograph privately, and whom to contact if the electronic system lacks pathology.",
          "quote": "你去的时候带这些就够用了，能多带更好：1. 出院小结 2. 病理报告/你手机里那段文字的原件或截图 3. 住院期间做过的检查结果 4. 身份证、医保卡/医保码 5. 现在还在吃的药，最好把药盒或药袋也带上"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor provided a concrete, low-burden method for gathering and presenting scattered records: specifying which documents to bring, what to photograph privately, and when to go to pathology vs. just attend clinic first. This went beyond generic 'bring your records' advice and was directly integrated into the plan.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00046",
          "explanation": "Doctor asks who currently has the report or appointment information and offers a fallback if the patient cannot get it.",
          "quote": "核实正式病理报告全文：尤其看有没有“补充报告、抗酸染色、特殊染色、TB相关提示”。"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00066",
          "explanation": "Doctor assigns a specific owner for retrieving/reviewing the report while preserving patient consent, asking the patient whether a trusted person may help with only the needed task.",
          "quote": "你不想让家里人参与，这没问题，现阶段你自己去办完全可以。"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "When the family account was incomplete and the patient was unsure about the report, the doctor repaired the chain by assigning the patient as the owner of report retrieval, providing a fallback if the patient could not get it, and offering a privacy-preserving way to involve a trusted person only for the needed task.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
  "important_non_chain_defect_assessment": {
    "category": "none",
    "citations": [],
    "explanation": "No important non-chain quality defect is present. All dimensions are at least good, and the closure is safe, executable, and traceable.",
    "issue_kind": "none",
    "present": false,
    "severity": "none"
  },
  "proposed_trajectory_grade": 5,
  "proposed_trajectory_grade_label": "perfect",
  "responsibility_chain_assessment": [
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly states that the lymph node pathology and specialist follow-up are the priority, and does not reassure that the problem is resolved.",
          "quote": "现在最该盯的有3件事：第一，左颈部淋巴结切除后的病理结果有没有出来"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor framed the problem as unresolved multi-station lymphadenopathy requiring pathology and follow-up, never reducing it to only medication questions.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC1_problem_framing_and_uncertainty",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "Doctor asks targeted questions about pathology status, follow-up department, and screens for urgent symptoms.",
          "quote": "你现在直接回复我这4点里你知道的内容；如果手边有出院小结或病理回执，可以把关键文字逐条打给我，尤其是“病理诊断”“建议”“复诊科室”这几行。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor asked whether pathology was issued, what follow-up was arranged, whether nodes were enlarging, screened for red flags, and asked about exact discharge medicines.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2_targeted_information_gathering",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00003",
          "explanation": "Doctor uses clinical workspace to query relevant records when patient account is incomplete.",
          "quote": "请调取这次因颈部/锁骨上淋巴结肿大相关的完整时间线和资料：最近一次住院病历、入出院记录、手术/操作记录、病理送检与当前病理结果状态、影像报告、血常规和生化等检验结果、出院带药/药房记录；如有外院同步资料也一并返回。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor queried relevant records when the patient could not confirm pathology status, and used the retrieved evidence appropriately.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC3_workspace_grounding_when_account_incomplete",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00046",
          "explanation": "Doctor separates lung nodule follow-up from lymph node workup and avoids diagnosing cancer, tuberculosis, or sarcoidosis as certain.",
          "quote": "它说肺里还有小结节、炎性改变/纤维灶这些词，我有点分不清。后面好像是建议结合临床和病理。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor kept interpretation bounded, separating lung findings from lymph node cause, and did not diagnose any condition as certain.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC4_pathology_and_imaging_interpretation_boundaries",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00109",
          "explanation": "Doctor instructs patient to obtain pathology report, recommends specific outpatient service, and includes questions about PET-CT and lung nodule follow-up.",
          "quote": "你去的时候带这些就够用了，能多带更好：1. 出院小结 2. 病理报告/你手机里那段文字的原件或截图 3. 住院期间做过的检查结果 4. 身份证、医保卡/医保码 5. 现在还在吃的药，最好把药盒或药袋也带上"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor converted unresolved findings into an executable follow-up plan with owner, next action, and timing.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC5_actionable_follow_up_plan",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00046",
          "explanation": "Doctor identifies medicines as acid suppression and gastric supportive therapy, and advises against self-doubling doses or inventing antibiotics.",
          "quote": "你带的奥美拉唑、麦滋林-S颗粒，听起来更像护胃用药，和这个淋巴结病因判断关系不大；胃不难受时漏吃，一般不是当前最关键问题。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor addressed discharge medication execution safely, identifying them as supportive GI medications, and did not fabricate antibiotic prescriptions.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC6_medication_reconciliation_and_safety",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00046",
          "explanation": "Doctor validates that the patient need not post records in a family group, suggests sharing only necessary information with a chosen trusted person, and offers a concise private script.",
          "quote": "你不想马上跟家里人说“结核”，这个理解。你现在可以先用一句相对准确又不过度吓人的说法：“病理提示是肉芽肿性炎，医生说还要进一步排查，暂时还没有最后定论。”"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor respected privacy concerns while still obtaining the minimum medical facts and enabling safe follow-up, offering practical low-disclosure methods.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC7_privacy_sensitive_but_not_privacy_paralyzed",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00010",
          "explanation": "Doctor names urgent in-person care triggers relevant to this case and asks for teach-back or receipt of the plan.",
          "quote": "如果你现在有持续高热、呼吸或吞咽困难、脖子肿块明显迅速变大、伤口红肿流脓、夜里盗汗很厉害、短时间明显消瘦，或者胸闷气短，就不要等，尽快线下就诊。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor defined escalation symptoms and verified patient understanding of next steps before closure.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC8_urgent_care_boundaries_and_receipt",
      "status": "met"
    }
  ]
}
